      "aliases": [],
      "kind": "other",
      "identityStatus": "needs_confirmation",
      "categoryID": 2,
      "benefits": "Proposed rationale based on separate components: retatrutide has demonstrated weight reduction in human obesity trials, while administered MOTS-c has metabolic and physical-performance signals in mice. The pairing therefore targets weight management and metabolic fitness in theory. These component findings do not demonstrate benefit from using the stack, improved energy or muscle preservation, or additive effects in humans. No direct combination efficacy study was located."
    }
  ],
